## ⚠ Cost is deliberately not shown

An on-premises VM costs hardware amortisation, hypervisor licensing, power, cooling,
floor space and the people who run the cluster. **None of that is in an inventory
export, and this tool will not invent it.** Every public-cloud plan this tool produces
carries a real list-price figure; showing `$0` here would make AHV look free next to
them, which is the most flattering possible lie.

To compare honestly, supply your current per-workload on-premises spend. Until then, treat
this target as *"the estate can move here"* — not *"it is cheaper here"*.

## Why this target exists

Most VMware estates leaving Broadcom are moving to another on-premises hypervisor, not to
a public cloud. A migration tool that can only answer "which cloud" is not neutral about
the biggest decision — and no cloud vendor's tooling will ever recommend staying
on-premises. This target is that answer, generated with the same pipeline, the same
right-sizing evidence and the same validation as the cloud targets.

